messages:
lina: FYI customer (ACME) hit a 400 on /v1/rerank. They sent a payload that sometimes has a trailing comma and an item with an empty candidates array. Full payload they pasted:
```json
{
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "q-123",
      "query": "best CRM integrations",
      "top_k": "5",
      "candidates": [],
    },
    {
      "id": "q-124",
      "query": "pricing info",
      "top_k": 3,
      "candidates": [
        {"id": "c1", "text": "Plan A"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
lina: The API responded with a parse error first: `Malformed JSON: Unexpected trailing comma at position 123` and then with a schema complaint when they removed the trailing comma: `400 Bad Request - items[0].candidates must be a non-empty array of objects`.
ajay: thanks — can you repro locally with their exact payload + curl?
lina: repro steps I used: 1) saved their payload to payload.json, 2) `curl -sS -X POST "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/rerank" -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" -H "Content-Type: application/json" --data-binary @payload.json` -> got the trailing comma parse error. Remove comma -> now hits our validation error about empty candidates.
kevin: two separate problems: (A) client-side JSON serialization bug adding trailing commas (common js stringify wrapper bug), (B) our schema acceptance allows empty candidates arrays but then rejects later; that leads to flaky error messages. We should tighten validation to fail earlier with clearer field path.
ajay: Agree. For immediate workaround for the customer: ask them to ensure candidates is either omitted or contains at least one candidate object with id/text. Also ask them to send top_k as an integer (their top_k is a string in item 0).
lina: Sent ACME this patch suggestion (quickfix in their Node SDK):
```diff
- body.items[i].top_k = String(body.items[i].top_k)
+ body.items[i].top_k = parseInt(body.items[i].top_k, 10)
```
lina: Also pointed them to a tiny preflight validate step we can share:
```js
function validate(items){
  if(!Array.isArray(items)) throw new Error('items must be array');
  items.forEach((it, idx)=>{
    if(!it.id) throw new Error(`items[${idx}].id required`);
    if(!Array.isArray(it.candidates) || it.candidates.length === 0) throw new Error(`items[${idx}].candidates must be non-empty array`);
  });
}
```
kevin: For the platform fix: 1) Update parser error handling to include byte offset and offending token (so trailing comma errors are actionable). 2) Change validation error to be returned at parse/validation stage with a single clear JSON path and example of expected type. 3) Add a short doc snippet in rerank API errors page. I can take 1 and 2.
ajay: please attach a minimal repro script and open an ENG ticket. Assign to eng-runtime.
kevin: Opening CORE-9876 with repro + curl + payload.json; will include suggested response strings for ops.
deploy-bot: Created issue CORE-9876: "rerank: improve JSON parse and candidates validation errors" assigned to eng-runtime.
lina: Thanks — I've asked ACME to try the SDK fix and run the validate() snippet. I'll follow up when they confirm.
ajay: :thumbsup:
kevin: follow-up note: we should also add a quick error code mapping in support KB so CS can give the right immediate guidance (trailing comma => client stringify bug; empty candidates => ensure at least one candidate object).
lina: copying the customer convo into the ticket. Closing this thread unless ACME reopens with new repro.
